  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q19-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "19",
    "prompt": "Solve the equation $2\\log_2(x+5)-\\log_2(x+9)=1$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=-1$\n\nCombine logarithms to form a quadratic, then reject roots outside the original logarithm domain.",
      "worked": "The domain requires $x+5>0$ and $x+9>0$, so $x>-5$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_2\\big((x+5)^2\\big)-\\log_2(x+9)&=1\\\\\\log_2\\left(\\frac{(x+5)^2}{x+9}\\right)&=1\\\\\\frac{(x+5)^2}{x+9}&=2\\\\(x+5)^2&=2(x+9)\\\\x^2+10x+25&=2x+18\\\\x^2+8x+7&=0\\\\(x+7)(x+1)&=0\\\\x&=-7\\text{ or }-1\\end{align*}$$\nReject $x=-7$ because $\\log_2(x+5)$ is undefined.\n\n$$x=-1$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
